=== layout: one-panel

# Group Presentation

@body

- Longer presentation\: [20-30 minutes in length]{color=#CC00CC}
  - you will be penalized if not with 10% of time
    - 18 &#8211; 33 minutes
- Every member has to talk for at least 3 minutes
- Videos
  - Videos are great
  - But you should be the narrator, wherever possible
  - Keep them short, less than 2 minutes

=== layout: one-panel

# Presentation Outline Suggestions

@body

- [The best presentations deviate from the outline guide and do their own thing]{color=red}
- It is better to introduce the group members one at a time as they are ready speak, rather than all at once.
- Choose an emcee (the most enthusiastic member) to run the show and introduce the other members for their subsections.
- It is better to bring back different members and interact
  - Don't just divide up the presentation into parts and go in linear order = boring!

=== layout: two-panels

# Pre-Recorded Videos

@left

- Pre-Recorded Videos are [ALLOWED]{color=green}
- They must follow all of the guidelines
- You must use your own voice, no playing videos or using AI generated voices
- The runtime is expected to be
  - within 10% of 20-30 minutes

@right

- Videos can be uploaded to [YouTube]{color=red} or uploaded to [Blackboard]{color=red} under Assignments.
  - Facebook, Quibi, TikTok are not allowed.
- Videos are due [Thursday, Dec 10 before 12PM noon]{color=red} (or Wed night) of the presentation day
  - Dr. Voss plans to download all of the videos (including from YouTube) to his desktop and play them from his computer to avoid internet connectivity issues.

=== layout: two-panels

# Suggested Presentation Outline

@left

- [The best presentations deviate from this outline]{color=red}
- Introduce problem in great detail
- Two members talk about science in great detail
  - switch back and forth between members for each slide
  - Looking for specifics
  - bonus if related to course material
  - this should be the focus of the presentation

@right

- Reveal the Product
  - Introduce your product as the solution to the problem
  - Talk about how your product is better than competition
- Marketing
  - Discuss size of the market; Talk about revenue projections
  - Show milestones and your plan to achieve them
  - recommend to keep this short, it is usually pretty boring
- Introduce team members as needed

